/**
 * @page commenting_conventions Doxygen Commenting Conventions
 *
 * ManuMesh documentation follows one contract-oriented style:
 *
 * - Every owned C/C++ file has `@file`, `@brief`, and `@ingroup` metadata.
 * - Public and cross-translation-unit declarations use `/** ... */` Doxygen
 *   blocks with an explicit `@brief`; `src/` does not mix line-style `///`
 *   or `//!` documentation comments.
 * - Parameters use `@param[in]`, `@param[out]`, or `@param[in,out]` whenever
 *   mutation or ownership is not obvious.
 * - Non-void functions state `@return`; status-valued functions also document
 *   important `@retval` cases.
 * - Exceptions, lifetime requirements, units, valid ranges, determinism, and
 *   thread-safety are part of the API contract and are documented explicitly.
 * - Algorithm entry points use `@algorithm`, `@complexity`, `@invariants`, and
 *   `@failuremodes` sections where those facts affect correct use or review.
 * - Short trailing data-member comments use `/**< ... */`; a preceding
 *   `/** ... */` block is used when units, range, ABI history, or interactions
 *   need more detail.
 *
 * Plain `//` comments inside a function are reserved for local proof
 * obligations, numeric derivations, and non-obvious implementation choices.
 * They intentionally remain ordinary source comments: changing them to
 * a documentation block would make Doxygen bind text to a local statement or variable
 * and would produce misleading API pages. Algorithm-wide explanations belong
 * on the function declaration or file page instead.
 */
